OrionLayer open fix 67 — the message box's item values on the wire
===================================================================

Work order 199 (Part C, step C4). orion2re a8381e60 on `orionlayer-local`, on
top of 121950ed (open fix 66). src/ext only.

WHAT IS MISSING. Open fix 29's MSGB sends a box's text raw, FMTPARA codes and
all. An item code (0x18, a letter, one hex digit: Insert_Item_,
fmtpara.cpp:854) prints a value the caller set with
Set_Paragraph_*_Pointer_ just before the box, which lives only in the
engine's memory. The boarding result ("Capture Star Base",
cmbtfir2.cpp:1640-1647) is made of them: the bonuses and the marines
before, killed and left. A client printed the codes' letters ("B6") or
nothing.

WHAT THE PATCH ADDS. MSGB's block version 2: after the title and the text, a
count byte, then for each item index the text names and whose pointer is
set, the index byte and its int32 value, read through the game's own
FMTPARA::Get_Item_Value_ while the box is up, which is while its caller's
variables are.

BEHAVIOUR WITHOUT ORIONLAYER: unchanged. The values are only read; nothing
in the game changes.

HOW TO REVERT. git revert a8381e60.

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
